From 5d10276ec92cbeefcaec3ab06165f23d48025f03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SHORiN-KIWATA <shorin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:10:06 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wintun: Implement the Wintun userspace tunnel driver
 interface.

Wintun lets a program create a TUN adapter and exchange packets with the
network stack through it. Implement the DLL on top of the unix TUN driver:
creating an adapter opens /dev/net/tun, the returned LUID is the one the
NDIS ifinfo table has for the new interface, so the iphlpapi interface,
address and route functions can be used on it, and a session exchanges
packets between the TUN device and buffers handed to the caller.

The structures passed to the unix library do not depend on the pointer
size, so the same functions serve 32-bit callers under WoW64.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
